# Copy to `.env` IN THIS DIRECTORY:  cp .env.example .env
# compose reads it automatically when you run `up -d` from here. `.env` is
# gitignored; THIS file is tracked and must never carry a real value.
#
# THIS FILE BELONGS TO THE MLFLOW GATEWAY ALONE. Each gateway is a standalone
# compose project with its own .env, so ../litellm and ../envoy have their own and
# can name a DIFFERENT engine. Nothing checks that they agree.
#
# THERE IS NO COMPOSE_PROFILES LINE ANY MORE. Before the split one word chose
# which gateway ran; now the directory you are standing in is that choice, and
# `up -d` here starts this gateway whether or not this file exists.
#
# THERE IS NO KEY VARIABLE FOR THE GATEWAY ITSELF EITHER. MLflow has no key
# concept: anything on 25000 is callable by anything that can reach the port.

# --- WHICH ENGINE ---------------------------------------------------------------
# ONE WORD, and it is the only thing that decides what this gateway serves. Five
# engines exist, one self-contained file each in config/:
#
#   lms          LMStudio, on this machine        free    lms-4b lms-26b lms-embed
#   unsloth      Unsloth Studio, on this machine  free    unsloth-4b -26b -embed
#   ollama       Ollama, on this machine          free    ollama-4b -26b -embed
#   openrouter   OpenRouter                       PAID    openrouter-26b
#   openai       OpenAI                           PAID    openai-mini openai-embed
#
# `openrouter-free` IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT HERE and exists only on the LiteLLM
# gateway. MLflow has no equivalent of `extra_body`, so it cannot carry the
# provider pin that route needs, and an unpinned copy would return tool calls as
# raw text — an agent that executes nothing and reports no error.
#
# ONE ENGINE AT A TIME. There is no list and no `all`. Every other engine's
# endpoints are simply not seeded, and a 404 on one is correct.
#
# SELECTING A PAID ENGINE IS THE ONLY WAY ANYTHING HERE CAN SPEND MONEY. The seed
# prints a PAID ENGINE line in its log when you pick one — `compose logs
# mlflow-seed` is where to look.
#
# A TYPO IS A CLEAN FAILURE: mlflow-seed exits 2 naming the bad word and listing
# the five valid ones. The server itself stays up, serving whatever it held before.
GATEWAY_ENGINE=lms

# --- WHICH MODELS: hand-written only, or every model on this machine -------------
# BLANK IS THE DEFAULT AND CHANGES NOTHING. This gateway then serves exactly the
# endpoints `config/<engine>.py` names, and that file stays in the repo as the
# worked example of how to configure this gateway by hand.
#
# SET IT TO `on` AND THE SEED ADDS EVERY MODEL THE ENGINE HOLDS. At `up -d` it asks
# the engine over its own HTTP API what is on the disk and APPENDS one endpoint per
# model. LMStudio and Ollama both report models that are NOT LOADED as well as
# loaded ones, and both JIT-load, so a not-loaded model answers on the first call.
#
# THE NAME IS THE ENGINE, A DASH, AND THE MODEL ID, with anything MLflow rejects
# turned into a dash. So `google/gemma-4-e4b` on LMStudio becomes:
#
#   lms-google-gemma-4-e4b        ollama-gemma4-26b        ollama-nomic-embed-text-latest
#
# IT ONLY EVER ADDS. The hand-written endpoints come first and a discovered alias
# that would collide with one is dropped, so `lms-4b` keeps meaning what it always
# meant. Turning this on cannot break anything a project already calls.
#
# DISCOVERY IS LOCAL-ONLY: `lms`, `unsloth` and `ollama`. Those are free, so a long
# list costs nothing. OpenRouter lists hundreds of models and every one bills a real
# account, so the two PAID engines keep their hand-written lists and MONEY IS NEVER
# DISCOVERED. Ask for discovery on one and the seed refuses by name.
#
# `off` DOES NOT MEAN OFF — the seed reads the word as non-empty, which means ON.
# It catches `off`, `false`, `0` and `no` and exits 2 telling you to blank the
# value. TO TURN IT OFF, LEAVE IT EMPTY.
#
# UNSLOTH REPORTS THE NAMES FINE — it is the numbers that are thin. Its /v1/models
# gives every model on disk with its `quant` and whether it is `loaded`, so the
# aliases are complete and correct. Two gaps, measured 2026-09-03 against 15 models:
# the context window comes only for the ONE LOADED model (14 of 15 rows were null),
# and there is no type field, so chat against embedding is guessed from the name.
GATEWAY_DISCOVERY=

# --- MLflow gateway -----------------------------------------------------------
# Wraps the key that encrypts the provider credentials MLflow stores in its
# database. Blank is supported: MLflow falls back to a built-in passphrase and
# writes a warning at startup. Fill it in for anything beyond a laptop.
#
# CHANGING IT LATER BREAKS THE STORED SECRETS. They were encrypted under the old
# value and stop decrypting, which shows up at CALL time as an auth failure, not
# at startup. The repair is `podman compose up -d`, because mlflow-seed rewrites
# every secret on each run.
MLFLOW_CRYPTO_KEK_PASSPHRASE=

# --- The three LOCAL engines --------------------------------------------------
# All three run NATIVELY on the host for the Apple-Silicon GPU, and all three bind
# 127.0.0.1 only. The containers still reach them at host.containers.internal
# (Podman) / host.docker.internal (Docker), so these lines rarely change.
LM_STUDIO_API_BASE=http://host.containers.internal:1234/v1
UNSLOTH_API_BASE=http://host.containers.internal:8888/v1
OLLAMA_API_BASE=http://host.containers.internal:11434/v1

# UNLIKE LMStudio, Unsloth REQUIRES a key: every route answers `401 Not
# authenticated` without one, `/v1/models` included. Make one in the app —
# avatar (bottom-left) -> Settings -> API -> Create — and note that it is shown
# only ONCE and is stored hashed, so a lost key is remade, never recovered.
#
# LEAVE THIS BLANK. It is a personal credential: put it in
# ~/.secrets/secrets.enc.yaml with `secret-edit` and let ~/Projects/.envrc export
# it.
#
# A BLANK VALUE HERE FAILS QUIETLY. The seed SKIPS every endpoint whose key is
# empty, saying "no API key in the environment", and MLflow never gets them — so
# the `unsloth-*` aliases 404 on 25000 with nothing obviously broken.
UNSLOTH_API_KEY=

# THERE IS NO OLLAMA_API_KEY, and nothing is missing: Ollama does not read the
# Authorization header at all. config/ollama.py still sets a literal `sk-ollama`
# on every endpoint, precisely because the seed skips an endpoint with an empty
# key.

# --- Hosted providers ---------------------------------------------------------
# The keys the two PAID engines bill. Neither engine is seeded at all unless
# GATEWAY_ENGINE names it. A missing key means the seed skips the endpoint, so the
# alias 404s here — the same missing key makes LiteLLM answer 401 instead.
#
# LEAVE THESE BLANK. They are personal credentials, not per-project config, and
# they already reach every shell under ~/Projects from ~/.secrets/secrets.enc.yaml
# through ~/Projects/.envrc. Compose reads the SHELL environment before this file,
# so a blank line here resolves to the real value at `up` time and no second
# plaintext copy is created.
#
# Only fill these in on a machine with no ~/Projects/.envrc (a CI runner, a
# colleague's laptop).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
